Z||000006||1FieroGTRacingInc||07-15-2000||12:39 AM||||Do the Indy scoop's ACTUALLY,help cool the engine compartment???  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||07-15-2000||12:46 AM||||My scoop keeps the engine compartment REALLY cool. The heat rises up the front side and is drawn out the vents and the Indy scoop forces air down the trunk side (back side) of the engine. I am going to eventually hook the Indy scoop to the engine and use the Holley side scoop to draw in cool air. With the original air cleaner assembly ouy of the way it should keep the engine comartment cool as well.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Oreif1_1.jpg"> <P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 07-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||007DOUG||07-15-2000||01:21 AM||||Are you talking about this pair?<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/t-toprear.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/t-toprear.jpg</A> <P>Oreif is correct, they are IRM, and are unavailable. Thats an IRM wing and ground effects on the car too.<P>IRM also has the Indy scoop:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/indy2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/indy2.jpg</A> <P>I have also seen a pair of scoop that are very much like IRM's, but they hang off to the side, rather than over the top. I think thats the Lazy-C that Old Lar is speaking of.<P>BroCar 87: Thats one sweet trunkild.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Gokart||07-15-2000||06:58 AM||||Unless you make it functional by connecting them to throttle body with air cleaner like Oreif's, those over head scoops will work against the natural air flow and you may over heat. I know cause I had those scoops that mounted on the side grills when FOCOA were selling them when I had an 85 2M4 5 years ago. I took bad advice and removed the thermo to keep from over heating. When I traded it in for a "family ride" I left the scoops on. I should've taken them cause they'd be worth even more now <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||4
Z||000010||fldevel||07-15-2000||12:05 PM||||the point of the scoops it to force air over the engine compartment ..as with the origonal grills if you look at them areodynamicaly they actualy form a pocket of air over the grills wich trap air in wich in turn reverses the airflow to whare it goes into the vents insted of out .. kinda an areodynamic push and pull , but they where origonaly designed to suck air in caused by the low pressure vaccume from under the car ..  ||||reg||1
